WEBVTT

00:10:27.081 --> 00:10:30.501
that you can't live with the people
that you want to live with most.

00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:33.379
How did we get here?

00:10:33.712 --> 00:10:37.132
How did we get to this supervised society?

00:10:38.258 --> 00:10:41.512
The roots run deep,
at least as deep as our country.

00:10:42.846 --> 00:10:45.349
But the legal infrastructure
for a supervised society

00:10:45.391 --> 00:10:47.059
began in the 1980s.

00:10:47.101 --> 00:10:48.894
It starts in housing policy.

00:10:49.311 --> 00:10:51.814
Congress passed legislation
that made it so

00:10:51.814 --> 00:10:55.818
that landlords would reject
applicants with criminal records,

00:10:55.859 --> 00:10:59.530
and people in public housing
had the power to evict tenants

00:10:59.571 --> 00:11:01.407
who allow people with criminal records